  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e2aca7f4-50e8-51f6-a422-185c74b96d2b" activityNameId="92b600de-7b77-5c0f-b1f5-90c2ac3c1006" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, redmud from bauxite digestion, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, redmud from bauxite digestion, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% redmud from bauxite digestion; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 379730; H n.a.; C 7606.7; S 800; N n.a.; P 1475; B 10; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F 1130; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 29; Ba n.a.; Cd 4.5; Co 22; Cr 750.97; Cu 36.742; Hg 0.025; Mn 363.32; Mo n.a.; Ni 5.4; Pb 14.142; Sb 0.3; Se 5; Sn n.a.; V 535.08; Zn 36.661; Be 0.7; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti 40203; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 104470; Fe 296420; Ca 22446; Al 84217; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na 59688; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. ;; UUID: 2955bf0c-36fe-4840-971b-4cbdf820857e
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2955bf0c-36fe-4840-971b-4cbdf820857e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
